  - gfs_readdir
    The returned entry is part of an internal buffer and may be overwritten
    or purged by a subsequent directory operation. The caller must copy the
    entry if it needs to retain it. A reentrant API, for example one named
    gfs_readdir_r, should be implemented for callers that need returned data
    to remain valid independently of the directory handle.
  - gfs_seekdir
  - gfs_telldir

- MT-safe APIs with exclusive-close requirement

  The per-object locks serialize operations on the same GFS_File or GFS_Dir.
  The following APIs are MT-safe when the caller ensures that no other
  operation is using the same object. They destroy the object, so they must
  be called only after all other operations have completed:

  - gfs_pio_close
  - gfs_pio_close_getgen
  - gfs_closedir

- MT not supported APIs

  - gfarm_initialize
  - gfarm_finalize

